00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.720
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:11.680
Today we are going to make the Mona Lisa and&nbsp;
other fictional characters come to life through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:17.520
this DeepFake technology that is able to create&nbsp;
more detailed videos than previous techniques.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:26.160
So, what are DeepFakes? Simple, we record a&nbsp;
video of ourselves, as you see me over here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:32.880
doing just that, and with this, we can make&nbsp;
a different person speak. What you see here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.640
is my favorite DeepFake application where&nbsp;
I became these movie characters and tried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:46.240
to make them come alive. Ideally, expressions, eye&nbsp;
movements and other gestures are also transferred.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:54.720
Some of them even work for animation movie&nbsp;
characters too. Absolutely lovely. This can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:02.080
and will create filmmaking much more accessible&nbsp;
for all of us, which I absolutely love. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:08.720
when it comes to real people, just imagine how&nbsp;
cool it would be to create a more smiling version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:17.200
of an actor without actually having to re-record&nbsp;
the scene. Or maybe even make legendary actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:25.920
