00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:32.160
as their younger selves, which is a true&nbsp;
triumph of technology. What a time to be alive!

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.360
Now, if you look at these results, these are&nbsp;
absolutely amazing, but the resolution of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:45.520
outputs is not the greatest. They don’t seem to&nbsp;
have enough fine details to look so convincing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.840
And here is where this new paper comes into play.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:59.200
Now, hold on to your papers and have a look at&nbsp;
this. Wow. Oh my! Yes, you are seeing correctly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:06.240
the authors claim that these are the first one&nbsp;
megapixel resolution deepfakes out there. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:12.800
means that they showcase considerably more&nbsp;
detail than the previous ones. I love these,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.280
the amount of detail compared to&nbsp;
previous works is simply stunning.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:24.320
But, as you see, these are not perfect by any&nbsp;
means. There is a price to be paid for these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:31.280
results. And the price is that we need to trade&nbsp;
some temporal coherence for these extra pixels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.720
What does that mean? It means that as&nbsp;
we move from one image to the next one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:42.640
the algorithm does not have a perfect memory of&nbsp;
what it had done before, and therefore some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:48.160
these jarring artifacts will appear. Now,&nbsp;
you are all experienced Fellow Scholars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:54.560
so here, you know that we have to invoke The&nbsp;
First Law Of Papers, which says that research&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:03:00.720
is a process. Do not look at where we are, look&nbsp;
at where we will be two more papers down the line.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.080
So, megapixel results huh? How&nbsp;
long do we have to wait for these?&nbsp;&nbsp;

